      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pulaski was named after Casimir Pulaski, a Polish-born general who fought for the Patriots during the American Revolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulaski%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was founded in 1809 and quickly grew into the county seat of Giles County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulaski%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic Downtown Pulaski blends its agricultural roots with charming streets, local shops, and makers proud of their craft.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpulaski.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The University of Tennessee Southern campus, formerly Martin Methodist College, sits in Pulaski and serves the region’s higher‑education needs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
